29	/* ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
30	   KODELY PRODUCT SURFACE
31	   ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
32	   The tokens above (--accent, --brand-gradient, --glow…) are the MARKETING
33	   system and are ported from the approved reference mockup. Do not repoint
34	   them; the marketing pages read them directly.
35	
36	   These are the PRODUCT tokens — the portal and the builder. They are additive
37	   and share the same brand hues on purpose, because a customer crosses
38	   marketing → portal → builder in one session and the seam should be
39	   invisible. What differs is density: marketing is a poster, the product is an
40	   instrument, so the product gets a surface ramp, semantic status colour, and
41	   a tighter spacing/type scale that the marketing pages have no use for.
42	
43	   TYPEFACE: deliberately still Geist. A display serif was considered and
44	   rejected — the marketing site the customer just came from is set in Geist,
45	   and swapping faces at the /dashboard boundary would break the one continuity
46	   requirement that matters most. "Premium" here is bought with the type SCALE,
47	   tracking, tabular numerals and weight discipline below, not a second family.
48	
49	   NEUTRALS are hue-biased toward the brand (a touch of magenta in light, a
50	   touch of indigo in dark) rather than pure grey, so panels sit in the same
51	   world as the accent instead of looking like a default admin theme. */
